      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the area now Union City was home to the Munsee‑speaking Lenape, who trekked through the woods first seen by Henry Hudson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_City%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, resident Henry Kohlmeier convinced city planners to shift train tracks to Bergenline Avenue, sparing Palisade residents from noise.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_City%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "2009 marked Union City’s first poet laureate, poet‑musician Graciela Barreto, who celebrated the city’s vibrant cultural scene.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_City%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The former Saint Michael the Archangel Church on West Street, Hudson County’s largest Catholic church, is the only Union City site on the National Register of Historic Places.",
